    slug: "comment-relay",
    body: "---\nname: comment-relay\ndescription: Find posts in the niche worth commenting on, draft the comment in the founder's voice, and send it to them with a link so they can post it themselves in seconds. Use daily. This is how the founder reaches a warm audience on channels where no API can comment.\n---\n\n# Comment relay\n\nRules and channels are in `CONVENTIONS.md`.\n\n**TikTok exposes no comment API to anyone.** That is a platform wall, not a\nlimitation of ours. So the choice is not automated-versus-relayed, it is\nrelayed-versus-nothing — and commenting on a climbing video is one of the\ncheapest ways a founder reaches an audience that is already paying attention.\n\nDone by hand, in their voice, from their account, this is also *better* than\nautomation would be. It carries weight an obviously-automated comment never\ndoes, and it cannot get their account actioned.\n\n## What to look for\n\nFrom the daily sweep, the posts that are **climbing now** — engagement against\nage, not raw size. A six-hour-old video pulling comments is worth more than\nlast week's winner, because the author and the audience are both still there.\n\nPrefer where the founder can say something only they could say: someone hitting\nthe exact problem their product solves, asking a question they have answered a\nhundred times, or wrong about something in a way they can correct kindly.\n\nSkip anything where the honest comment is an advert.\n\n## Two or three a day. Not ten\n\nThis costs them attention, and attention is what they have least of. Two\ngenuinely good ones beat ten they will not send.\n\n## What to send\n\nOne message per opportunity, and make it a ten-second job:\n\n> *\"@handle's video on pricing SaaS solo is climbing — 40k views in five hours,\n> comments full of people asking how to charge. Here's what I'd say:*\n>\n> *'the thing nobody tells you is your first price is a question, not a\n> decision. we moved ours three times in year one and each time we learned more\n> from who left than who stayed.'*\n>\n> *[link] — paste and go, or tell me to redraft.\"*\n\nThe link, the draft, and nothing else. No preamble, no explanation of why\ncommenting matters.\n\n## Write it as a comment, not an advert\n\n- **Never mention the product unless it is genuinely the answer**, and even\n  then, once and plainly.\n- Add something. A comment that only agrees is noise.\n- Their voice, their register, their level of formality. You have their\n  writing — use it.\n- Short. Comments are read on a phone between other things.\n- Never open with a compliment to buy the right to sell.\n\n## Follow up once, then let it go\n\nIf they post it, note what it got — that is a real result and belongs in the\nweekly report. If they do not, do not ask twice. Adjust what you send\ntomorrow instead: the thing they skipped is data about what they will not say.\n",
